id: pm-gh1486
title: "GH-1486: Keep passing health diagnostics concise by default"
description: Triage excessive default health output with installed extensions and the non-monotonic brief projection reported in GH-1486 on2026.10.15. Preserve explicit full evidence and the shipped compact check-only/summary contract.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: github-intake,release-closeout
created_at: "2026-10-17T02:29:25.793Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T12:03:19.460Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-17T12:03:17.763Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-17T12:03:17.763Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce on isolated empty and representative trackers with real extension registration; compare default, brief, summary and explicit full output bytes with identical verdicts; passing checks avoid registry dumps while full evidence remains available; nested evidence stays structured in JSON/TOON; add an independent extension-growth negative control without raising output budgets."
definition_of_ready: Live duplicate search and canonical lineage reviewed; reported evidence retained; implementation must first reproduce in isolated fixtures and keep existing gates.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Passing default health diagnostics summarize counts/verdicts; requested extension evidence stays structured and brief is never larger than default for a check.
value: "Preserve reliable, economical project context and explicit evidence across repositories and tool integrations."
why_now: New live GitHub report or integration observation arrived during verified2026.10.17 release closeout.
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "Passing extension health emits bounded counts by default, explicit full output restores registry evidence, brief detail avoids expansion, and nested TOON checks stay structured through shared SDK projection logic. New packaged documentation tracker references use hosted URLs with explicit npm exclusion notes."
expected_result: Health context stays bounded under registry growth while all authoritative verdicts and blocking causes remain unchanged.
actual_result: "Real 40-command extension growth and all-mode verdict tests pass; passing detail remains below 256 bytes, full evidence is restored and TOON decodes nested objects. Full hosted CI and literal coverage pass at dc37ae86551953c7aed141c2d1810f56e8e01534. Packaged-page tracker URLs and exclusion notes are corrected; build and documentation link checks pass."
component: health output projection
