comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T02:29:25.793Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: Live search1486 and health output plus open/in-progress inventories found no owner for this new report. Read completed pm-nbht and pm-du93sr and the open budget parentpm-5t33or; retain their shipped contracts and link the new default/brief intake as distinct residual scope."
  "2026-10-17T09:13:25.453Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: reproduce real extension-growth output in isolated trackers; preserve summary/check-only and explicit full evidence, authoritative verdicts and actionable warnings. Bundle related SDK read-context defects pm-gh1481 and pm-gh1482; no output budget or quality threshold increase."
  "2026-10-17T09:22:11.799Z","harness:codex","SDK compatibility decision: the previously implicit default evidence projection now has an additive standard discriminator; brief, summary and explicit full remain supported. The conservative SDK signature gate requires a recorded acknowledgement for union widening; updated its snapshot with that exact rationale. Full results and authoritative verdicts are preserved; no public symbol was removed."
  "2026-10-17T09:38:51.569Z","harness:codex","Verification found the existing health-file and integration-directory ceilings. Extract projection logic into a focused SDK module and place the new real-boundary regression under tests/integration/read-output; preserve all file/directory, coverage and output-token thresholds. Chrome also confirms no open Semgrep findings match pm-cli main after refresh."
  "2026-10-17T09:57:04.104Z","harness:codex","Final focused acceptance passes for count-only healthy extension details, explicit full restoration, authoritative verdict equality, UTF-8 byte non-expansion per brief check, and structured TOON round trips. Projection implementation is in src/sdk/governance/health/projection.ts so the health engine remains below the existing implementation-line ceiling; the fixture under read-output restores the directory cap. No quality ceiling was raised."
  "2026-10-17T10:41:25.936Z","harness:codex","Current production revision passed the complete local functional suite: 819 files, 10575 tests, three existing skips. Literal coverage correctly refused two newly exposed migration-summary lines after removing the old exclusion; added a behavioral case proving migration counts survive without record expansion or input mutation, and the focused health suite passes 63/63. No ignores, denominator, deadlines or thresholds changed. Final full-source coverage and unchanged static admission will be required from the hosted PR head before closing this cohort. Three independent integration regressions fail against the original revision at their intended defects; same-surface source-mutant controls also pass."
  "2026-10-17T12:03:16.527Z","harness:codex","Final package-content inspection found three new tracker references pointing at repository files excluded from npm. Changed the new references in COMMANDS and OUTPUT_PROJECTION_CONTRACTS to canonical hosted GitHub file URLs and stated the exclusion beside them, preserving relative links between packaged pages. Build and focused documentation link checks pass; runtime source remains identical to the verified dc37 head."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T10:17:03.771Z","harness:codex","Linked-test trust is pinned to source provenance. Inspect the exact stored commands, acknowledge them in a separate non-executing --acknowledge-linked-tests invocation, then run them normally; this preserves project trust policy without allowing arbitrary untrusted commands."
